# Trivy ignore allowlist for bigcapital-fork.
#
# The deploy gate (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) is HIGH/CRITICAL + ignore-unfixed,
# exit-code 1 (blocks deploys). This file is the explicit, dated BASELINE of the
# pre-existing server-image debt that the gate-flip (2026-05-31) ratcheted over:
# every NEW HIGH/CRITICAL now blocks; the entries below are tracked, justified,
# and expiry-dated for quarterly review. The webapp image is clean (0).
#
# Before the flip, a devDependency-leak cleanup cut findings 155 -> 105 and
# removed all but one CRITICAL via Dockerfile + dep-categorization fixes and a
# handful of safe same-major pnpm overrides (form-data, fast-xml-parser,
# cross-spawn, fast-uri, validator). See docs/CI-CD.md.
#
# Policy for entries:
#   - Add ONLY a fixable HIGH/CRITICAL that is (a) transitive/cross-major we
#     can't safely bump without breaking a pinning SDK, or (b) unreachable in
#     our runtime, or (c) build-time-only. Comment the why + an expiry date.
#   - Revisit every entry at/*before* expiry; remove once the dep is bumped
#     past the affected version. Shrinking this file is the goal.
#   - A bare entry with no justification/expiry is a bug — root-cause first.
#   - Re-scan recipe: docs/CI-CD.md ("Trivy CVE findings").

# ── @casl/ability 5.4.4 — CRITICAL prototype pollution; fixed in 6.x (MAJOR).
#    Authorization engine; the v6 bump rewrites Ability APIs and needs careful
#    permission-check QA. Tracked for a dedicated bump. Expires: 2026-08-31
CVE-2026-1774

